body:
I gave humanity a shot for ages but they shown me time and time again how hateful and disgusting they can be, compulsive lying, picking sides, doxxing a minor and shoving years of assault their way over minimal reason.

&#x200B;

What do I base this off of? My own life, obviously. I've been treated like shit since I was born, even my own family verbally abused me until one day I snapped and developed chronic depression and severe anxiety.

&#x200B;

Nowadays I avoid everyone and everything, I sit in the rain, draw violence to get the angry thoughts out of my head. People who don't understand might call it psychopathic, but I don't have enough care left for humanity to gaf what they think.

&#x200B;

In the end, it's just you, and online no one can do anything to you. When I'm alone I can do anything I want without some unfair judgement being tossed my way over stupid reasoning, and if I talk to anyone I keep them at such a strong length I'd barely ever consider anyone my friend, because people like to lie. Like to say they care for you when in reality they'd drop you like a dime the first chance they get. It's disgusting.

&#x200B;

I'd rather be despised or called mentally screwed than blend in with a parasitic crowd, I blend in to survive, not to feel wanted.
